      "content": "Figure 3-9: Side-by-side placement of 400 ~ 500 kVA UPS rectifier cabinet and inverter cabinet"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0232",
      "reading_order": 274,
      "section": "3.3.3 Cabinet Parallel Installation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 74.664,
        "t": 490.39766291015627,
        "r": 541.2747199999995,
        "b": 449.72610136319497
      },
      "content": "Fixed  installation:  disassembly  the  back  board  of  cabinets  placed  side  by  side.  Fix  the  two cabinets together with screw rod at the \"fixing holes for parallel connection of the two cabinets\" (as shown in Figure 3-10), and then fit on the back board."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0233",
      "reading_order": 275,
      "section": "3.3.3 Cabinet Parallel Installation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 74.664,
        "t": 180.02766291015632,
        "r": 541.61566,
        "b": 139.35610136319497
      },
      "content": "Bus connection: connect the bus of rectifier cabinet with soft copper bar (as shown in Figure 3-11) and then correspondingly connect it to the copper bars for the bus of inverter cabinet (as shown in Figure 3-12)."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0234",
      "reading_order": 276,
      "section": "3.3.3 Cabinet Parallel Installation",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 101.18,
        "t": 120.62766291015623,
        "r": 397.83567999999997,
        "b": 111.15610136319492
      },
      "content": "Note: +BUS, N and -BUS must be connected correspondingly."
    },
